        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Buy continuous horsepower, size it to your
            weight as well as your pace, and stop once you have a margin.</strong>
            2.5 CHP walks, 3.0 CHP jogs, 3.5 CHP runs daily — plus a quarter
            horsepower per 50 lb above 200. Any figure that does not say
            continuous is worth roughly half what it claims.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
            With the motor settled, the next number that changes how the machine
            feels is deck size — see the
            <a href="/treadmill-belt-size-guide/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">belt size guide</a>
            — and the one that decides whether it fits at all is in
            <a href="/treadmill-dimensions-space-requirements/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">dimensions and space requirements</a>.
          </p>
